  "solution": "The logic followed here is : **Square of 2nd number = (1st number + 3rd number)**\n\nGiven :\n\n \n• \n \n(25, 9, 56)\n\n \n\n(9)² = 25 + 56\n\n81 = 81 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• \n \n(13, 14, 183)\n\n \n\n​(14)² = 13 + 183\n\n196 = 196 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (42, 12, 228)\n\n​(12)² = 42 + 228\n\n144 ≠ 270 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (11, 16, 135)​\n\n​(16)² = 11 + 135\n\n256 ≠ 146 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (19, 23, 511)​\n\n​(23)² = 19 + 511\n\n529 ≠ 530 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (27, 15, 198)​\n\n​(15)² = 27 + 198\n\n**225 = 225 (LHS = RHS)**\n\nHence, **\"Option - (4)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n \n\n58:Tf11,\n<p",
